# J14 — Narrow terminal (responsive matrix)
# Exercise the canonical Target → Setup → Run Focus spine at 60x20. For the
# other live matrix cells, re-run with --size 80x24 or --size 96x89.
name: Responsive cockpit spine
size: 60x20
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch:
wait-for: 2 CHOOSE A TARGET
snap: narrow-target
expect: Enter selects
ask: At this terminal size, is explicit Target consent readable without clipping its selected identity or controls?
keys: Enter
wait-for: 3 SETUP · READY THE MAP RUN
snap: narrow-setup
expect: Map plan
expect: Model
expect: NOT NEEDED
expect: Credentials
expect: Budget
expect: Start Map
ask: Does aggregate Setup keep every readiness dependency and the single Start Map commit reachable at this terminal size?
keys: Down
wait: 0.1
keys: Down
wait: 0.1
keys: Down
wait: 0.1
keys: Down
wait: 0.1
keys: Down
wait: 0.1
keys: Down
wait: 0.1
keys: Enter
wait-snap: 5 TASKS | narrow-run-focus
expect: TASKS
expect: OUTPUT
expect-not: kuzushi>
ask: Does Run Focus use its responsive TASKS/OUTPUT geometry without reserving the generic shell prompt or a blank canyon?
wait-for: 30 run receipt
snap: narrow-setup-receipt
expect: SETUP · READY THE MAP RUN
expect: run receipt
ask: Did terminal completion restore the exact Setup origin with one durable receipt and no background focus theft?
